.TH APP 5
.SH NAME
app \- the desktop's app launchers (.app files)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/apps/*.app
.br
.B ~/*.app
.SH DESCRIPTION
An app is a small text file ending in
.BR .app ,
of
.IB key = value
lines;
.B #
starts a comment.
Everyone's apps are in
.BR /etc/apps ;
a user's own are any
.B .app
file in their home folder.
The desktop,
.BR atlas (4),
lists them in the Deskbar's menu and the sia strip, and Files starts one
when it is opened.
.TP
.B name
what the strip and the menus show (none: the file's name)
.TP
.B run
the program, an absolute path
.TP
.B args
its arguments, one line
.TP
.B kind
.B terminal
(the default): runs in a new terminal;
.BR editor :
opens the editor on an empty, untitled file;
.BR settings :
opens Settings;
.BR git :
the Git window;
.BR mail :
opens Mail;
.BR camera :
the Camera window;
.BR install :
the Install window;
.BR window :
a program that opens its own window (its terminal waits minimized).
.PP
Starting an app opens a terminal as the user logged in, never root; its
shell runs the app's command when it first asks for a line.
When the app ends, the shell stays
.RB ( exit
closes it).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# A SIEOS app launcher (docs/desktop.md): key=value lines.
name=Hello
run=/bin/hello
args=from an app
kind=terminal
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR atlas (4),
.BR hier (7)
